      image: "/locations/hutton.png",

      description:
        "Hutton is the land of the Orcs. No one truly knows how big this city is as it delves deep into the side of the Grey Mountains. This land is known for its rich mining colonies and abundant natural gems, ores and magical artifacts. Some say the mountain mines lead into the underworld, though none have ever verifiably confirmed the truth of this claim. From a young age, Orcs growing up in this land are taught the importance of wealth, almost to the point of obsession. Despite this, the Orcs of Hutton tend not to hoard their gold, instead preferring to trade ore for gold and gold then for better mining equipment, in the hopes of finding the “Hut-Hut Gem”, a mythical artifact of incredible power that their forefathers once searched for. None remember now why this artifact was so important, but the search continues, nonetheless.",
      lore:
        "",

      ruler:`
      The Marquess Mulchch
      
      Mulchch is widely disliked for her micromanaging attitude to working the mines. Her great-great-great-great-great-great-great grandmother Gurghgh fought tooth and nail against the mountain Wargs for these mountains and now that she is in power, she will stop at nothing to find the “Hut-Hut Gem”. The Marquess Mulchch is conventionally extremely unattractive to most non-Orcs, though to Orcs, she is a figure of divine beauty. She stands at 7 feet tall, with matted black hair and a scarred, greyish face. She has long silver hoop earrings and more piercings that it would be polite to count. She is polite to outsiders but will refuse to back down from any disagreements, even if she knows that she is in the wrong.

      `,

